{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1116786-what-happens-if-you-go-loud-and-your-already-primum-10","id":1116786,"title":"What happens if you go loud and your already Primum 10 ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-16T03:58:24-07:00","id":1116786,"title":"What happens if you go loud and your already Primum 10 ?","content":"So I was talking with one of my players and they wanted to know what would happen if a demon who is already Primum 10 went loud. Looking at the rules It does not seem like there would be much benefit for them.<br /> <br /> So I've come here to see if I could ask some other GM's if they any ideas of what should happen at that level ?<br /> <br /> Me and the other player started spit balling ideas such as creating fusions of embeds and exploits to get new effects. Maybe at High levels of Primum a demon can go loud and still hide from gods eye for turns equal to their Primum level<br /> <br /> Me and the other player were also spit balling ideas for Fractals. They thought it would be cool if they could get access to exploits but doing so gives them a catastrophic glitch. Warping their body making them look more demonic. Worse still, using an exploit, regardless of success or fail on a compromise roll automatically causes at least a minor glitch. For a scene<br /> <br /> Also do you think the next demon book will cover rules for high level demons ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 07-16-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:10:43-07:00","id":1116791,"title":"","content":"You do heal every bashing &amp; lethal damage, Tilts, and spent Aether by Going Loud, so a demon low on Health and Aether could still benefit from it. Destroying a Cover for sure is another use of Going Loud, should that be needed.<br /> <br /> I'll have to think a bit more for any benefits on top of them. Perhaps some Merits that build on Going Loud?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:43:30-07:00","id":1116799,"title":"","content":"You also get all the embeds for your incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T06:05:58-07:00","id":1116819,"title":"","content":"And every Exploit.<br /> <br /> Really, increased Primum is just about the least important benefit of Going Loud. It gives you a big bonus to those Exploits and a lot of Aether to play with, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1116786-what-happens-if-you-go-loud-and-your-already-primum-10?p=1116791#post1116791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do heal every bashing &amp; lethal damage, Tilts, and spent Aether by Going Loud, so a demon low on Health and Aether could still benefit from it. Destroying a Cover for sure is another use of Going Loud, should that be needed.<br /> <br /> I'll have to think a bit more for any benefits on top of them. Perhaps some Merits that build on Going Loud?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it's your last Cover, you can just let go of any Cover you don't want any more at no cost. <i>Flowers of Hell</i>, p.30","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-16-2017, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:07:19-07:00","id":1116855,"title":"","content":"I think I made a few Merits for these situations on the Homebrew Demon Merits thread.<br /> <br /> So there is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\">this</a> set (I really need to finish Occult Experimentation and Institutional Cover), and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848219#post848219\">these</a> two, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=932094#post932094\">Suborned Facility</a>.<br /> They aren't really tied to Primum 10 or Going Loud, but rather high Primum in general.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=881817#post881817\">Phoenix Pattern</a> grants benefits when Going Loud the more Embeds and Exploits the Demon knows at 3 dots, and let's them scavenge more Cover at 4 dots.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=881817#post881817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Phoenix Pattern</u> \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Demon [Add other Pre-reqs? Primum?]<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have fine tuned and optimized the dangerous technique of Going Loud, figuring out how to wring even more power out of the process.<br /> <i>Immolation</i> (\u2022): When Going Loud, the Demon deals their Cover in Lethal Damage to everything in Primum yards, as they shred their Cover in a conflagration of Aether. The Demon can choose to exclude targets from this eruption.<br /> <i>Surging Fire</i> (\u2022\u2022): When Going Loud, the Demon can spend Aether as if it were Willpower to add dice to rolls, or bolster their Resistance (though they can only do this once per roll). This stacks with any Willpower spent on the same roll or Resistance.<br /> <i>Glorious Rise</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): When Going Loud, all Embeds and Exploits the Demon possessed beforehand are rolled as Rote actions.<br /> <i>From the Ashes</i> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): When Going Loud, a Demon can harvest some of the fading cosmic power to reconstruct a Cover. The Scene <i>after</i> the one where they went Loud, the Demon can create a new Patchwork Cover at a rating equal to their spent Cover - 1, or their Primum, whichever is less.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The first dot is like a Saboteur's Self-Destruct for everyone, but in addition to Going Loud instead of replacing it. Not tied to it, but it fits thematically. I capped the second dot because Demons can spend 15 Aether when Loud, and 48 (16*3) to dice pools or -32 (16*2) to Resistance roll is <i>crazy</i>, even if it would blow your Aether stores. Third dot is for Demon's that invest in Incarnation Embeds and Exploits get a benefit when Going Loud, instead of having their prior choice made redundant. Fourth dot is the reason for the whole thing, mitigating part of Going Loud's cost, while favoring higher Primum Demons (who get less benefit from the Primum = 10). Primum = Cover dots is pretty big, though, so maybe reducing it to giving Cover Experiences? That would mean a Demon at Primum 9+ can create a Cover 3 Patch-Job afterwards.]</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then there are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1012643#post1012643\">these</a>, for upgrading Factals.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=1012643#post1012643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Demonic Heir (\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Offspring or Fractal<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your tie to your demonic ancestry has strengthened to the point where you can now develop some of the inherent traits and characteristics of your Unchained Forebears. You can acquire Demon Merits as if you were a Demon, provided you can meet the rest of the prerequisites.<br /> <b>Note:</b> This merit costs 3 dots for Fractals, and 5 dots for Offspring. Offspring who acquire it are also treated as if they were Fractals for the purposes of eligibility for other merits, but not their costs. You are treated as if you had Primum 1 for prerequisites that call for Primum. If you acquire a Demonic Form Ability (such as through Terrible Form), you can conduct a Partial Transformation, except it also deals 1 point of Lethal Damage to express a Form Ability.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This is a simple effect with wider consequences. With it, you could pick up Terrible Form to acquire Form Abilities (the &quot;extras&quot; would be added to your current totals of 0), grab your own Bolthole somewhere (and somehow), Talk &quot;machine&quot; with Electromagnetic Linguistics, tattoo yourself with Embedded Gadgets, etc. The Primum requirement of some merits automatically excludes some of the odder edge cases from consideration.]<br /> <br /> <b>Exploiter (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Demonic Heir, Ambient Aether or Aether Pool, Intelligence 3, Occult 3, Successfully Overcharged a prerequisite Embed, not Activated<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your potent ancestry and repeated experiments with the God-Machine's occult hacks has unlocked the secret of reliably supercharging those tricks into a powerful Exploit. You gain the use of an Exploit each time this Merit is acquired.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> In addition to the typical consequences of Compromise, each use of the Exploit is tied to a transient Glitch the Demon-blooded suffers when using it (instead of the usual Condition the Compromise roll inflicts). Exception Success negates acquiring the Glitch for that roll.<br /> <b>Note:</b> This Merit covers access to an Exploit, as if the Demon-blooded where at Primum 1. They still must supply Aether to fuel the Exploit, and still risk Compromise.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: I priced it at 4XP, because I thought Demon-Blooded picked up Embeds at increased cost, but I didn't see that anywhere on a reread. The &quot;Not Activated&quot; requirement is because I doubt the Machine would approve of its tools messing around with Exploits, and the Compromise risk loses its sting at that point.]<br /> <br /> <b>Pact-Maker (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Demonic Heir<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can harness the reality altering nature of Pacts, albeit to a limited degree. You can swap and transpose Cover elements, automatically integrating them into your life, but you cannot grant a person new traits in exchange for such details. You may exchange Merits with a Pactee (often Social) using the normal rules regarding the Pact's Benefits and Costs. While you <i>can</i> also create Soul Pacts, you only have one identity, so your previous one fades into oblivion if you assume another's.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Really leery on this one. Pact Making seems a bit strong and tied to Primum, but the concept of a person exchanging parts of their lives with others is tempting.]</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, and on the Glitch note for Fractals (or Offspring) - if you don't feel like dealing with their Cypher, I've debated using Glitch acquisition instead (too?) for failed Compromise rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-16-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}